Wine win32u: AlphaBlend with per-pixel alpha and full constant alpha, which every gdiplus image and text draw goes through, blends four pixels at a time with SSE2 and writes the same bytes as the scalar code, falling back to it where a colour above its alpha carries into the next channel. The FSLabs displays spent about 7% of the simulator's cycles in this loop.
Applies to wine-cachyos with: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 -i <this file>

